{# COVER / editorial_hero (bottom-anchored).

   The headline rests ON the meta block rather than floating mid-canvas, and the
   open area above it is framed by the full-bleed accent rail so it reads as
   composition. A cover legitimately needs room for its headline to land - what was
   wrong with the original frames was not open space but that every frame had the
   SAME open space in the same place.

   `at-bottom` is what distinguishes this from big-text, which uses `at-centre`. In
   the first pass both were bottom-anchored and came out near-identical. #}
<div class="lay L-hero at-bottom" style="--headline-len: {{ view.headline_len }};">

  <div class="hero-rail"></div>

  <div class="hero-eyebrow region">
    {% if slide.eyebrow %}<div class="sec-eyebrow">{{ slide.eyebrow }}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="hero-body region">
    <h1 class="hero-headline">{{ slide.headline }}</h1>
    {% if slide.subheadline %}<p class="hero-sub">{{ slide.subheadline }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="hero-swipe region">
    {% if totalSlides > 1 %}<span class="swipe">Swipe &rarr;</span>{% endif %}
  </div>

  {% include 'partials/meta.njk' %}

</div>

<style>
  /* The swipe affordance gets its own grid row so it cannot collide with either
     the headline above or the source line below. */
  .L-hero .hero-swipe { padding: 34px 96px 0 96px; }
</style>
